{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JHN",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After these things Jesus walked in Galilee: for he would not walk in Judea, because the Jews sought to kill him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the Jews' feast of tabernacles was at hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His brethren therefore said to him, Depart hence, and go into Judea, that thy disciples also may see the works that thou doest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doeth any thing in secret, and he himself seeketh to be known openly. If thou doest these things, show thyself to the world.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For neither did his brethren believe in him.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Jesus said to them, My time is not yet come: but your time is always ready.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The world cannot hate you; but me it hateth, because I testify concerning it, that its works are evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go ye up to this feast: I go not yet to this feast, for my time is not yet full come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he had said these words to them, he abode ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "still",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in Galilee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But when his brethren had gone up, then he went also to the feast, not openly, but as it were in secret.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the Jews sought him at the feast, and said, Where is he?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there was much murmuring among the people concerning him: for some said, He is a good man: others said, No; but he deceiveth the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet, no man spoke openly of him, for fear of the Jews.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now about the midst of the feast, Jesus went up into the temple, and taught.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the Jews marveled, saying, How knoweth this man letters, having never learned?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus answered them, and said, My doctrine is not mine, but his that sent me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man will do his will, he shall know concerning the doctrine, whether it is from God, or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whether",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I speak from myself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that speaketh from himself, seeketh his own glory: but he that seeketh his glory that sent him, the same is true, and no unrighteousness is in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Did not Moses give you the law, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none of you keepeth the law? Why go ye about to kill me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The people answered and said, Thou hast a demon: who goeth about to kill thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus answered and said to them, I have done one work, and ye all marvel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moses therefore gave to you circumcision, (not because it is from Moses, but from the fathers) and ye on the sabbath circumcise a man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If a man on the sabbath receiveth circumcision, that the law of Moses should not be broken; are ye angry at me, because I have restored a man to sound health on the sabbath?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Judge not according to the appearance, but judge righteous judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said some of them of Jerusalem, Is not this he whom they seek to kill?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But lo, he speaketh boldly, and they say nothing to him. Do the rulers know indeed that this is the very Christ?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But we know this man, whence he is: whereas when Christ cometh, no man knoweth whence he is.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then cried Jesus in the temple, as he taught, saying, Ye both know me, and ye know whence I am: and I am not come of myself, but he that sent me is true, whom ye know not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I know him; for I am from him, and he hath sent me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they sought to take him: but no man laid hands on him, because his hour was not yet come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And many of the people believed on him, and said, When Christ cometh, will he do more miracles than these which this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hath done?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Pharisees heard that the people murmured such things concerning him: and the Pharisees and the chief priests sent officers to take him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said Jesus to them, Yet a little while am I with you, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I go to him that sent me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye will seek me, and will not find ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": and where I am, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thither",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye cannot come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said the Jews among themselves, Whither will he go, that we shall not find him? will he go to the dispersed among the Gentiles, and teach the Gentiles?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "manner of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " saying is this that he said, Ye will seek me, and will not find ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": and where I am, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thither",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye cannot come?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the last day, that great ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the feast, Jesus stood and cried, saying, If any man thirsteth, let him come to me, and drink.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that believeth on me, as the scripture hath said, out of his belly shall flow rivers of living water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(But this he spoke of the Spirit, which they that believe on him should receive, for the Holy Spirit was not yet ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "given",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", because that Jesus was not yet glorified.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Many of the people therefore, when they heard this saying, said, In truth this is the Prophet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Others said, This is the Christ. But some said, Will Christ come out of Galilee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hath not the scripture said, That Christ cometh from the seed of David, and out of the town of Bethlehem, where David was?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So there was a division among the people because of him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And some of them would have taken him; but no man laid hands on him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came the officers to the chief priests and Pharisees; and they said to them, Why have ye not brought him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The officers answered, Never man spoke like this man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the Pharisees answered them, Are ye also deceived?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have any of the rulers, or of the Pharisees believed on him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But this people who know not the law are cursed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nicodemus saith to them, (he that came to Jesus by night, being one of them)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth our law judge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " man before it heareth him, and knoweth what he doeth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They answered and said to him, Art thou also from Galilee? Search, and look: for out of Galilee ariseth no prophet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.7.53",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.7.53",
      "verse": 53,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And every man went to his own house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
